== P1: AeST source verification (arXiv:2007.00082 newRMONDLett.tex; arXiv:2304.05134 main.tex)
  found   action Eq.5: R - K_B/2 F^2 + 2(2-K_B) J.dphi - (2-K_B) Y - F(Y,Q) - lambda(A.A+1)
  found   J_mu = A^alpha nabla_alpha A_mu (aether acceleration)
  found   Q = A^mu d_mu phi, Y = q^{mu nu} d phi d phi
  found   K(Qbar) = -1/2 F(0,Qbar)
  found   J -> 2 lambda_s/(3(1+lambda_s) a0) Y^{3/2}
  found   Gt = (1 - K_B/2) G_qs
  found   G_N = (1 + 1/lambda_s) G_qs (tracking; screening = lambda_s -> inf)
  found   mu = sqrt(2 K2/(2-K_B)) Q0
  found   vectors healthy if 0<K_B<2 and lambda_s>-1
  found   scalar requires K2>0
  found   omega=0 mode requires lambda_s>0
  found   lambda_s influences the effective cosmological gravitational strength
  found   VSZ: G_qs = G_N/(1+beta_0)
  found   VSZ: lambda_s = 1/beta_0
  found   VSZ: Minkowski stability lambda_s>0, mu^2>0
  discrepancy/note: real_research/bridge1_aest_equations.md: matches the source on every load-bearing item checked (action, lambda_s coefficient, Gt = (1-K_B/2) G_qs, mu, the E equation); it omits J_mu = A^a nabla_a A_mu and K = -F(0,Q)/2 (omissions, not errors).
  discrepancy/note: real_research/THE_NEXT_CALCULATION_aest_quasistatic.md: writes F(Y,Q) = -K(Q) + ...; the source has F(0,Q) = -2 K(Q) (K = -F(0,Q)/2, PRL text after Eq. 5).
  discrepancy/note: C1 (covariant_push_2026_10_22/C1_aest_embedding/README.md, point 1): takes the mass term as K2 Q0^2 Psi^2 in 16 pi Gt L, m^2 = K2 Q0^2/(2-K_B), and calls the record's 2K2 'a convention'. With K = -F(0,Q)/2 the source fixes (2-K_B) mu^2 = 2 K2 Q0^2 (Eq. 6): C1's m^2 is mu^2/2 (a factor-2 slip in C1; it touches only the Mpc-scale mass term, not C1's verdict).
  discrepancy/note: C1 K2: G_N = 2 Gt/(2-K_B) at lambda_s -> inf agrees with the source; the 'Newtonian regime as a cap' is the screening limit lambda_s -> inf, which the source equates with screening.
P1 PASS 15/15 found all found
== P2: G_cosmo/G_N in AeST and the A78 BBN line g > 0.9611
  g = Gt/G_N = lambda_s*(2 - K_B)/(2*(lambda_s + 1));  residual vs (1-K_B/2) lambda_s/(1+lambda_s) = 0
  BBN: K_B < 0.0778 (lambda_s -> inf), lambda_s > 24.707 (K_B -> 0); jointly (1-K_B/2) lambda_s/(1+lambda_s) > 0.9611
  VSZ's plotted lambda_s = 1, 2, 10 give g <= 0.500, 0.667, 0.909 (Delta N_eff = -3.72, -2.48, -0.68; A78 line |Delta N_eff| < 0.30); SZ's CMB 'MOND models' have lambda_s = inf
